  "_about": "a striped skunk SCULPTED on its rig (2026-11-05, gen: scratchpad sc/new6/skunk.py): small, stocky and low, the back arched highest over the hips, short legs, a small pointed head; long coarse black fur, a thin white stripe up the forehead, a white cap on the crown and nape that splits at the shoulders into two broad white bands along the upper flanks to the rump -- painted per pixel (the `skunk` pattern) on the trunk and head; a long round plume of a tail carried up and arched over the back, black with a white streak along its top and a white tip SHARP PASS 2 (2026-11-08): the pointed parts -- claw (3 in all) -- are the engine's sharp `horn`s (sharp.js), made from the field shapes they replaced by tools/creaturegen/sharp/ (claws.py, teeth.py, spikes.py, antlers.py, bills.py): rooted in the body, tips pointed; RE-RUN those after this species' generator. (2026-11-08, review.py: claws) The claws RE-ROOTED (review.py): each a sheath as wide as the claw where it leaves the toe, sunk in it, the join faired (horn `fair`: grown out of the skin in its paint), darker at the base fading to its own colour at the point -- no pale cut edge where it leaves the fur. (2026-11-08, ears2.py) The EARS (ears2.py): small round cupped sheets (sharp.js `fin`); the roots faired.",
